prison on one hand,

269
00:34:03.835 --> 00:34:05.461
and leaving the state
on the other.

270
00:34:06.796 --> 00:34:08.131
That's an easy choice.

271
00:34:23.062 --> 00:34:24.313
Try not to talk

272
00:34:24.397 --> 00:34:26.357
unless he directly
asks you a question,

273
00:34:26.441 --> 00:34:27.483
which he won't.

274
00:34:27.775 --> 00:34:29.402
Just like we talked about,

275
00:34:29.485 --> 00:34:30.485
he'll ask what you plead,

276
00:34:30.528 --> 00:34:32.989
you say guilty, and this
will be over quick enough.

277
00:34:36.409 --> 00:34:38.035
"<i>the said
Richard Perry Loving,</i>

278
00:34:38.327 --> 00:34:39.912
"being a white person,

279
00:34:39.996 --> 00:34:42.248
"and the said
Mildred Dolores Jeter,

280
00:34:42.331 --> 00:34:43.833
"being a colored person,

281
00:34:43.916 --> 00:34:46.085
"did unlawfully
and feloniously,

282
00:34:46.169 --> 00:34:48.087
"go out of the state
of Virginia,

283
00:34:48.171 --> 00:34:49.922
"for the purpose
of being married

284
00:34:50.006 --> 00:34:51.758
"in the District
of Columbia,

285
00:34:51.841 --> 00:34:54.218
"on June 2nd, 1958,

286
00:34:54.761 --> 00:34:56.596
"and afterwards returned to,

287
00:34:56.679 --> 00:34:59.390
"and resided in the
County of Caroline,

288
00:34:59.474 --> 00:35:01.017
"State of Virginia,

289
00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:03.436
"cohabitating as
man and wife,

290
00:35:03.519 --> 00:35:06.481
"against the peace and dignity
of the Commonwealth."

291
00:35:08.691 --> 00:35:09.859
How do you plead?

292
00:35:14.155 --> 00:35:15.156
Guilty.

293
00:35:18.284 --> 00:35:19.285
Guilty.

294
00:35:20.036 --> 00:35:22.455
The court does accept
the plea of guilty,

295
00:35:23.164 --> 00:35:25.374
and fixed the punishment
of both accused

296
00:35:26.042 --> 00:35:27.376
at one year in jail.

297
00:35:29.712 --> 00:35:31.714
The court does suspend
said sentence

298
00:35:32.423 --> 00:35:34.675
for the period of 25 years,

299
00:35:34.759 --> 00:35:36.719
upon the provision
that both the accused

300
00:35:36.803 --> 00:35:39.388
leave Caroline County and the
State of Virginia at once.

301
00:35:40.056 --> 00:35:42.809
And do not return
together at the same time

302
00:35:42.892 --> 00:35:44.393
to said county and state

303
00:35:45.061 --> 00:35:46.729
for a period of 25 years.

304
00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:50.483
Do either of you have
anything to say?

305
00:35:52.568 --> 00:35:53.569
No, sir.

306
00:35:55.404 --> 00:35:56.405
No, sir.

307
00:35:57.323 --> 00:35:59.923
You are released from custody.
Settle your court costs with clerk.

308
00:36:01.202 --> 00:36:02.411
Thank you, Your Honor.

309
00:36:05.081 --> 00:36:07.041
<i>It's 36 dollars</i>

310
00:36:07.124 --> 00:36:09.335
and 29 cents apiece.

311
00:36:25.393 --> 00:36:28.271
That's a number in
Washington for Nancy's brother Alex.

312
00:36:29.564 --> 00:36:31.607
His wife Laura's
there most days.

313
00:36:34.610 --> 00:36:36.279
If you need to get us,
just call.

314
00:36:36.946 --> 00:36:37.947
Okay.

315
00:36:48.082 --> 00:36:49.083
Daddy?

316
00:36:53.129 --> 00:36:54.130
You okay?

317
00:37:06.017 --> 00:37:08.477
You knew what you was doing
taking her up there!

318
00:37:09.729 --> 00:37:11.314
You had no right for that!

319
00:37:28.080 --> 00:37:29.081
Bean?

320
00:40:13.704 --> 00:40:14.705
How you all doing?

321
00:40:15.039 --> 00:40:16.332
We're fine.

322
00:40:17.166 --> 00:40:18.417
Thank you for taking us.

323
00:40:19.168 --> 00:40:20.544
We've got plenty of room.

324
00:40:21.295 --> 00:40:22.922
You remember Richard?
Yes.

325
00:40:23.923 --> 00:40:24.965
Thank you.

326
00:40:25.049 --> 00:40:26.467
No. Glad to have you.

327
00:40:27.551 --> 00:40:29.220
Come on in. Let me
show you the house.

328
00:40:47.488 --> 00:40:50.116
Yeah, they live, like, what,
two blocks over there, right?

329
00:40:50.199 --> 00:40:51.450
I know them.

330
00:41:34.410 --> 00:41:35.411
Okay.

331
00:41:53.596 --> 00:41:55.055
I'll be back by dinner.

332
00:43:12.549 --> 00:43:14.949
<i>If the vehicle
goes aloft at too step an angle,</i>

333
00:43:15.010 --> 00:43:17.554
<i>its velocity is cut by
800 feet a second.</i>

334
00:43:17.638 --> 00:43:20.349
<i>Working more directly
against gravity than planned.</i>

335
00:43:20.432 --> 00:43:22.685
<i>Reaching over 23,000
miles an hour,</i>

336
00:43:22.768 --> 00:43:24.937
<i>it carries to nearly
80,000 miles.</i>

337
00:43:25.020 --> 00:43:27.314
<i>Thirty times as far
as ever before...</i>

338
00:43:27.398 --> 00:43:28.565
<i>Another moon shot is...</i>

339
00:43:52.131 --> 00:43:53.132
What can I do?

340
00:43:56.635 --> 00:43:57.636
Nothing.

341
00:43:59.138 --> 00:44:00.139
Bean.

342
00:44:04.101 --> 00:44:05.102
It's just...

343
00:44:10.357 --> 00:44:12.484
I always thought your
mother would be the woman

344
00:44:12.568 --> 00:44:13.569
to deliver the baby.

345
00:44:23.370 --> 00:44:24.371
Damn it.

346
00:44:32.671 --> 00:44:33.714
Okay.

347
00:44:39.470 --> 00:44:40.512
Okay.

348
00:48:07.803 --> 00:48:09.555
Hey, Momma.

349
00:48:09.638 --> 00:48:11.598
Put some wood in the stove.

350
00:48:32.119 --> 00:48:33.620
Thank you for doing this.

351
00:48:35.956 --> 00:48:36.999
All right.

352
00:48:47.384 --> 00:48:49.303
All right, String Bean,
it's on you now.

353
00:48:53.056 --> 00:48:54.891
Yes, it is.
Drink this.

354
00:49:11.658 --> 00:49:12.659
Rich!

355
00:49:15.037 --> 00:49:16.038
Rich!

356
00:49:20.876 --> 00:49:22.961
Her water broke.

357
00:49:29.217 --> 00:49:31.428
Okay. Take a breath.
Take a breath.

358
00:49:35.098 --> 00:49:36.558
Breathe.

359
00:49:39.311 --> 00:49:40.771
Okay. Bear down.

360
00:49:41.313 --> 00:49:42.564
Bear down hard.

361
00:50:04.711 --> 00:50:05.962
Thank you, Momma.

362
00:50:10.467 --> 00:50:12.761
You never should
have married that girl.

363
00:50:17.516 --> 00:50:19.184
Well, I thought
you liked her.

364
00:50:20.686 --> 00:50:22.104
I like a lot of people.

365
00:50:23.271 --> 00:50:26.024
That doesn't mean you should
have gone and done what you did.

366
00:50:27.651 --> 00:50:29.069
You knew better.

367
00:50:46.670 --> 00:50:48.130
Sidney.

368
00:50:49.464 --> 00:50:50.924
Hi, Sidney.

369
00:50:55.137 --> 00:50:56.471
Sidney.

370
00:51:42.267 --> 00:51:43.602
Call the lawyer.

371
00:52:19.054 --> 00:52:20.722
Tell that woman
to come out here.

372
00:52:26.895 --> 00:52:28.063
She ain't here.

373
00:52:30.398 --> 00:52:31.608
She left.

374
00:52:31.691 --> 00:52:34.277
Boy, I will split your
head into white meat,

375
00:52:35.946 --> 00:52:38.073
and go arrest every
soul in that house.

376
00:52:43.119 --> 00:52:44.663
I won't ask you again.

377
00:53:05.851 --> 00:53:06.852
No.

378
00:54:18.048 --> 00:54:19.341
You are in luck.

379
00:54:20.508 --> 00:54:22.177
The Judge is in today.

380
00:54:23.929 --> 00:54:25.305
You'll go straight there.

381
00:54:31.269 --> 00:54:32.854
For violation
of your parole,

382
00:54:33.647 --> 00:54:35.941
you are ordered to
post a $200 bond,

383
00:54:36.983 --> 00:54:38.693
and appear
before this court...

384
00:54:38.777 --> 00:54:39.903
In the next...

385
00:54:47.702 --> 00:54:48.745
Yes, Frank?

386
00:54:50.038 --> 00:54:53.041
We ask for leniency.

387
00:54:53.959 --> 00:54:55.627
I incorrectly
told the Lovings

388
00:54:55.710 --> 00:54:57.212
it was fine for
them to return home

389
00:54:57.295 --> 00:54:58.463
for the birth
of their child.

390
00:54:58.546 --> 00:55:01.967
It... It was
my mistake.

391
00:55:08.765 --> 00:55:10.308
Your Honor, I think...

392
00:55:22.404 --> 00:55:23.530
Fine.

393
00:55:45.051 --> 00:55:46.219
Thank you.

394
00:55:49.305 --> 00:55:50.682
Don't come
back here again.

395
00:55:52.058 --> 00:55:53.560
You do and you
go to prison.

396
00:55:54.978 --> 00:55:56.521
This doesn't happen
a second time.

397
00:57:23.358 --> 00:57:26.027
Sidney, Donald,
come on down.

398
00:57:27.779 --> 00:57:28.947
Hey!

399
00:57:31.074 --> 00:57:32.158
Okay.

400
00:57:33.326 --> 00:57:35.036
Okay.

401
00:57:40.708 --> 00:57:42.043
Come on in.

402
00:57:47.632 --> 00:57:49.008
You go.

403
00:57:49.092 --> 00:57:50.301
Hi, pretty girl.

404
00:57:53.513 --> 00:57:56.432
Your cousin, Gerald
and Davis, are fine,

405
00:57:56.558 --> 00:57:59.394
and Sue and Terry
send their love.

406
00:57:59.477 --> 00:58:01.688
They just had
a little girl, too.

407
00:58:02.355 --> 00:58:04.816
Really?
Their second.

408
00:58:04.899 --> 00:58:05.900
Hmm.

409
00:58:07.485 --> 00:58:09.404
Sidney, don't jump
in the house.

410
00:58:12.073 --> 00:58:13.491
They're big.

411
00:58:15.743 --> 00:58:17.287
Yes.

412
00:58:19.330 --> 00:58:20.874
I hate it for them.

413
00:58:22.917 --> 00:58:23.918
It's like they're caged.

414
00:58:27.130 --> 00:58:29.215
Not even any grass
for them to run in.

415
00:58:32.218 --> 00:58:33.344
And Daddy?

416
00:58:33.928 --> 00:58:37.223
He's fine. Stays up in that
chair more than in the field.

417
00:58:37.932 --> 00:58:40.226
I told Momma if he don't start
getting some work done,

418
00:58:40.310 --> 00:58:42.854
Mr. Banks liable to find
someone else for it.

419
00:58:42.937 --> 00:58:45.648
Clay said he'd have to stay
with me until after the party.

420
00:59:13.509 --> 00:59:17.388
Good. How are you doing?
Where is that piece?

421
00:59:18.806 --> 00:59:20.308
How was your sister?

422
00:59:21.309 --> 00:59:23.519
I need one piece.
She's fine.

423
00:59:29.943 --> 00:59:33.238
I almost have it.
Yeah? You wanna show me?

424
00:59:33.321 --> 00:59:36.366
<i>The long awaited
march for jobs and freedom</i>

425
00:59:36.449 --> 00:59:38.451
<i>on Washington D.C.,
has started</i>

426
00:59:38.534 --> 00:59:42.455
<i>and it's about half of the
100,000 estimated crowd</i>

427
00:59:42.538 --> 00:59:46.084
<i>headed off down Constitution
Avenue toward the Lincoln Memorial</i>

428
00:59:46.167 --> 00:59:48.253
<i>which is where
we're seated now.</i>

429
00:59:48.336 --> 00:59:50.713
<i>It is here that the
climax of the march...</i>

430
00:59:50.797 --> 00:59:53.758
You boys stop that wrestling.

431
00:59:53.841 --> 00:59:55.927
Come and help Miss Laura
with her groceries.

432
00:59:56.386 --> 00:59:59.681
<i>Coming in around the plaza
surrounding Lincoln Memorial.</i>

433
01:00:01.182 --> 01:00:03.059
They say over 100,000
people are there.

434
01:00:03.518 --> 01:00:07.563
<i>Is standing by along the parade
route at 17th and Constitution.</i>

435
01:00:07.730 --> 01:00:08.856
Can you imagine?

436
01:00:10.942 --> 01:00:13.611
Might as well be half
way around the world.

437
01:00:13.695 --> 01:00:15.071
What?

438
01:00:16.364 --> 01:00:17.532
Nothing.

439
01:00:21.035 --> 01:00:22.429
You know what
you need to do?

440
01:00:22.453 --> 01:00:23.579
What?

441
01:00:24.747 --> 01:00:26.124
You need to write
Bobby Kennedy.

442
01:00:27.417 --> 01:00:28.710
I'm serious.

443
01:00:29.544 --> 01:00:31.421
I mean, that's what
they up there for.

444
01:00:31.504 --> 01:00:33.715
All this talk
of civil rights.

445
01:00:33.798 --> 01:00:35.591
You need to get you
some civil rights.

446
01:00:35.675 --> 01:00:37.969
<i>Engaged in
demonstrations before.</i>

447
01:00:38.052 --> 01:00:40.888
<i>In the background, you can hear
some of the young people shouting.</i>

448
01:00:42.890 --> 01:00:44.684
<i>"Freedom, freedom now."</i>

449
01:01:51.334 --> 01:01:52.335
Mmm.

450
01:01:58.299 --> 01:02:00.176
They in bed?
Mmm-hmm.

451
01:02:01.969 --> 01:02:03.346
I'm sorry I missed them.

452
01:02:04.972 --> 01:02:06.766
They ask for me?

453
01:02:06.849 --> 01:02:08.142
Peggy did,

454
01:02:09.102 --> 01:02:10.436
but she went down fine.

455
01:02:13.981 --> 01:02:15.400
Will you get Saturday off?

456
01:02:18.069 --> 01:02:19.362
I hope so.

457
01:02:37.880 --> 01:02:39.640
Sidney, get up and strip
those sheets for me.

458
01:02:39.674 --> 01:02:42.343
My turn, my turn,
my turn! My turn.

459
01:02:42.718 --> 01:02:45.179
Don, make sure your
sister gets a turn.

460
01:02:45.263 --> 01:02:47.265
My turn, my turn, my turn.

461
01:02:51.811 --> 01:02:53.062
Byrd residence.

462
01:02:53.980 --> 01:02:56.357
<i>Hello, I'm calling
to speak to Mildred Loving.</i>

463
01:03:01.195 --> 01:03:02.947
This is she.

464
01:03:03.030 --> 01:03:05.450
<i>Hello, Mrs. Loving,
my name is Bernard Cohen,</i>

465
01:03:05.533 --> 01:03:08.327
<i>I'm the lawyer that was
referred to you by the ACLU.</i>

466
01:03:08.411 --> 01:03:10.413
<i>Are you familiar?</i>

467
01:03:10.496 --> 01:03:12.206
I'm sorry. No.

468
01:03:12.290 --> 01:03:15.543
<i>You wrote a letter to Attorney
General Kennedy, is that right?</i>

469
01:03:17.420 --> 01:03:18.754
Yes.

470
01:03:18.838 --> 01:03:21.299
<i>He was not able to help you
with your particular case,</i>

471
01:03:21.382 --> 01:03:24.135
<i>and sent your letter to the
American Civil Liberties Union.</i>

472
01:03:24.218 --> 01:03:27.013
<i>The ACLU contacted me,
I'm a lawyer in Virginia,</i>

473
01:03:27.096 --> 01:03:28.890
<i>and we would like to
help you with your case.</i>

474
01:03:31.851 --> 01:03:33.311
I see.

475
01:03:33.394 --> 01:03:36.814
Momma! Momma!
Don, baby, hush.

476
01:03:38.065 --> 01:03:41.360
<i>Would it be possible for you
and your husband to meet with me?</i>

477
01:03:45.948 --> 01:03:48.034
I would have to
check with my husband.

478
01:03:49.660 --> 01:03:51.496
<i>Okay.
I'm based in Alexandria,</i>

479
01:03:51.579 --> 01:03:54.457
<i>but I have an office in D.C.
if that is a concern.</i>

480
01:03:55.750 --> 01:03:59.587
Well, as I said in my letter,
we really can't afford a lawyer.

481
01:03:59.670 --> 01:04:02.673
<i>No, ma'am. The ACLU
will take care of any fees.</i>

482
01:04:09.138 --> 01:04:11.224
<i>Mrs. Loving? Are you there?</i>

483
01:04:14.352 --> 01:04:17.063
- Yes, we'll see you.
<i>- Wonderful.</i>

484
01:04:17.146 --> 01:04:20.191
<i>I'll have my secretary call
you back to set up a time.</i>

485
01:04:20.274 --> 01:04:22.276
<i>Nice speaking with you,
Mrs. Loving.</i>

486
01:04:35.498 --> 01:04:36.749
Come here, baby.

487
01:04:39.377 --> 01:04:41.003
I got a call from
a lawyer today.

488
01:04:43.965 --> 01:04:46.217
A lawyer?
Mmm-hmm.

489
01:04:46.300 --> 01:04:49.303
From the American
Civil Liberties Union.

490
01:04:49.387 --> 01:04:51.222
Robert Kennedy
told him to call us.

491
01:04:52.473 --> 01:04:54.183
Go help your sister
brush her teeth.

492
01:04:56.852 --> 01:04:58.688
They wanna help
with our case.

493
01:04:59.814 --> 01:05:02.191
Well, we can't
afford a lawyer.

494
01:05:02.275 --> 01:05:03.693
He said they
wouldn't charge us.

495
01:05:06.195 --> 01:05:08.864
I'm gonna go
see him on Thursday.

496
01:05:08.948 --> 01:05:10.199
His name is Cohen.

497
01:05:33.723 --> 01:05:35.516
Hello.

498
01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:37.393
I'm Bernard Cohen.
I'm in from Richmond.

499
01:05:37.476 --> 01:05:39.770
I talked to Jim about using
his office for a few hours.

500
01:05:39.854 --> 01:05:41.105
Yes, Mr. Cohen,
do you know it?

501
01:05:41.188 --> 01:05:42.523
Down the hall?
Yes.

502
01:05:44.775 --> 01:05:46.402
My clients are
Mr. and Mrs. Loving.

503
01:05:46.485 --> 01:05:47.879
Could you send them
down when they arrive?

504
01:05:47.903 --> 01:05:49.030
Certainly.

505
01:06:29.862 --> 01:06:31.030
Come in.

506
01:06:34.575 --> 01:06:35.993
Mrs. Loving.
Hello.

507
01:06:36.077 --> 01:06:37.370
Please, have a seat.

508
01:06:38.204 --> 01:06:41.040
Bernard Cohen.
It's a pleasure.

509
01:06:45.419 --> 01:06:46.754
Thank you for
coming in today.

510
01:06:48.172 --> 01:06:49.882
So, as we discussed
on the phone,

511
01:06:49.965 --> 01:06:52.301
the ACLU would like
to take on your case.

512
01:06:52.385 --> 01:06:55.304
I was actually a charter member
of the ACLU in Virginia,

513
01:06:55.388 --> 01:06:57.306
which is why they
assigned me to you.

514
01:06:57.765 --> 01:07:01.102
The bottom line is, we wanna
get you all some relief.

515
01:07:03.437 --> 01:07:06.232
That's very generous.
Thank you.

516
01:07:06.315 --> 01:07:10.069
Now, the first step is to appeal
the sentence in Caroline County.

517
01:07:10.236 --> 01:07:12.988
That will be our fastest
route to Federal Court.

518
01:07:13.072 --> 01:07:14.740
The problem is...
Federal Court?

519
01:07:15.950 --> 01:07:18.953
Yes, the goal is to try to get the
Federal Court to hear the case...

520
01:07:19.036 --> 01:07:21.831
Excuse me, I don't understand...
Federal Court.

521
01:07:23.165 --> 01:07:24.583
I see it as the best route...

522
01:07:24.667 --> 01:07:27.211
Can't you just go and
speak to Judge Bazile?

523
01:07:28.129 --> 01:07:29.964
I mean, we ain't
hurting anybody.

524
01:07:30.339 --> 01:07:32.591
I don't think that...
Well, just talk to him.

525
01:07:32.675 --> 01:07:34.135
Just talk to him.

526
01:07:35.136 --> 01:07:37.972
Just tell him if he lets
us back in the state,

527
01:07:40.141 --> 01:07:41.517
we won't bother anybody.

528
01:07:47.481 --> 01:07:50.526
Look, I do not think
that this case

529
01:07:50.609 --> 01:07:52.903
will be resolved in
Judge Bazile's court,

530
01:07:52.987 --> 01:07:56.240
or probably any other court
in the state of Virginia.

531
01:07:56.323 --> 01:07:57.908
I believe this
is a court battle

532
01:07:57.992 --> 01:08:00.745
that could go all the way
to the Supreme Court.

533
01:08:09.003 --> 01:08:10.254
We're listening.

534
01:08:14.383 --> 01:08:17.762
Our problem is that in order to
appeal the judgment of conviction,

535
01:08:17.845 --> 01:08:20.431
we would have needed to
do so within 60 days.

536
01:08:20.514 --> 01:08:23.934
Now, given that it's been five
years since that conviction,

537
01:08:24.018 --> 01:08:26.854
we have to find a way to get
it back into the courts.

538
01:08:26.937 --> 01:08:28.898
Are you following?
Mmm-hmm.

539
01:08:28.981 --> 01:08:30.524
Mmm-hmm.

540
01:08:30.608 --> 01:08:32.276
Now, I've given
this some thought,

541
01:08:32.359 --> 01:08:36.238
and I have a somewhat unorthodox
idea on how to do this.

542
01:08:36.697 --> 01:08:40.659
My suggestion would be for the two
of you to return to Caroline County,

543
01:08:40.743 --> 01:08:45.289
get re-arrested, and then we will
have an avenue for our appeal.

544
01:08:50.419 --> 01:08:52.338
You want us to
get arrested again?

545
01:08:53.506 --> 01:08:54.632
Yes. It's an idea.

546
01:08:54.715 --> 01:08:56.550
I, of course, will be
there to bail you out.

547
01:09:03.557 --> 01:09:05.100
We aren't gonna do that.

548
01:09:07.895 --> 01:09:09.021
Right...

549
01:09:11.273 --> 01:09:13.108
I can see how
that was a mistake.

550
01:09:14.819 --> 01:09:16.028
I understand.

551
01:09:18.072 --> 01:09:22.034
Look, I need to do some more
thinking on this first issue, but,

552
01:09:22.117 --> 01:09:24.912
bottom line is we are gonna
get you all some help.

553
01:09:31.377 --> 01:09:32.628
We appreciate you.

554
01:09:34.380 --> 01:09:35.631
We really do.

555
01:09:38.717 --> 01:09:39.760
Yeah.

556
01:10:23.512 --> 01:10:25.639
If it gets us home,
we'll take their help.

557
01:10:28.267 --> 01:10:31.562
Well, you get
what you pay for.

558
01:10:47.620 --> 01:10:48.746
Get off the street!

559
01:11:08.515 --> 01:11:09.683
Lee, give him a hand!

560
01:11:19.985 --> 01:11:22.446
You gotta pull
that concrete. Yeah.

561
01:11:22.529 --> 01:11:23.530
Pull more.

562
01:11:26.450 --> 01:11:28.202
- Whoo-hoo!
- I got it!

563
01:11:29.536 --> 01:11:30.537
Hey!

564
01:11:30.871 --> 01:11:32.331
Look out!

565
01:11:38.253 --> 01:11:39.254
Donald!

566
01:11:46.136 --> 01:11:47.388
Momma!

567
01:11:48.472 --> 01:11:49.515
Momma!

568
01:12:40.441 --> 01:12:42.359
- Mildred!
- Up here!

569
01:12:50.784 --> 01:12:51.827
What's going on?

570
01:12:52.703 --> 01:12:54.496
Donald got hit
by a car today.

571
01:12:57.750 --> 01:12:58.917
What?

572
01:12:59.001 --> 01:13:00.419
He's fine.

573
01:13:02.463 --> 01:13:04.506
Just scraped
and bruised is all.

574
01:13:13.640 --> 01:13:14.641
Hey.

575
01:13:15.768 --> 01:13:16.769
You okay?

576
01:13:37.915 --> 01:13:39.917
I wanna move 'em back
to the country.

577
01:13:45.881 --> 01:13:47.883
I don't care what
they do to us.

578
01:13:52.638 --> 01:13:54.515
I won't raise my family here.

579
01:15:02.708 --> 01:15:05.377
All right. Y'all get loaded up now.
Come on.

580
01:15:05.586 --> 01:15:06.670
Thank you, Al.

581
01:15:06.753 --> 01:15:07.921
Thank you, Don.

582
01:15:10.007 --> 01:15:11.175
Thank you, Miss Laura.

583
01:15:11.258 --> 01:15:12.384
Hmm.

584
01:15:16.263 --> 01:15:17.514
You just go on.

585
01:15:31.820 --> 01:15:33.447
I'll see you tonight.

586
01:15:35.449 --> 01:15:38.160
- You all be good.
- Okay, Daddy.

587
01:16:41.807 --> 01:16:42.808
Hey.

588
01:17:06.915 --> 01:17:08.667
Daddy!

589
01:17:27.227 --> 01:17:29.271
My cousin has a house
he might rent out.

590
01:17:29.563 --> 01:17:32.065
But I thought Jim's brother
said it was fine here.

591
01:17:33.066 --> 01:17:36.069
I don't trust them.
Too many people.

592
01:17:39.740 --> 01:17:40.741
Where is it?

593
01:17:41.074 --> 01:17:42.409
King and Queen County.

594
01:17:42.951 --> 01:17:44.578
Just a farmhouse up there.

595
01:17:45.245 --> 01:17:47.485
I figure it gets you out the
county, but keeps you close.

596
01:17:47.998 --> 01:17:49.183
You'll be on your
own out there.

597
01:17:49.207 --> 01:17:50.834
It don't have no
phone or nothing,

598
01:17:50.917 --> 01:17:53.503
but no one's gonna find you
unless they know to look.

599
01:17:54.421 --> 01:17:56.214
I can get word to you
when you need it.

600
01:17:57.299 --> 01:17:58.884
How much you think
he'd want for it?

601
01:17:59.885 --> 01:18:01.053
Ah, he'll be fair.

602
01:18:59.653 --> 01:19:00.821
Hey, look.

603
01:19:08.912 --> 01:19:10.163
Peggy!

604
01:19:55.333 --> 01:19:56.334
Hey.

605
01:19:57.752 --> 01:19:59.463
I'll try and get home
before dark.

606
01:19:59.546 --> 01:20:00.547
Mmm-hmm.

607
01:20:02.340 --> 01:20:03.467
We'll be fine.

608
01:20:13.810 --> 01:20:15.228
"We haven't heard
anything from you

609
01:20:15.312 --> 01:20:17.147
"for so long
we had given up hope."

610
01:20:26.573 --> 01:20:29.367
Martha, call Chet Antieau's
office at Georgetown Law

611
01:20:29.451 --> 01:20:30.702
and try to set a meeting.

612
01:20:30.785 --> 01:20:32.120
<i>Yes, Mr. Cohen.</i>

613
01:20:35.499 --> 01:20:36.791
Come in.

614
01:20:37.375 --> 01:20:39.544
I'd never seen anything
like it, you know.

615
01:20:39.628 --> 01:20:40.837
Excuse me.

616
01:20:40.921 --> 01:20:42.398
No matter how many times
I get down south,

617
01:20:42.422 --> 01:20:44.102
there's always something
that surprises me.

618
01:20:45.300 --> 01:20:47.594
Oh, yes.
Please bring him back.

619
01:20:47.928 --> 01:20:49.012
This is good timing.

620
01:20:49.095 --> 01:20:51.056
I want you to meet
a former student of mine.

621
01:20:51.139 --> 01:20:53.183
He called about a case
you may find interesting.

622
01:20:54.935 --> 01:20:56.353
Yeah, sure.
What's it about?

623
01:20:56.436 --> 01:20:58.855
Well, we only spoke
briefly on the phone,

624
01:20:58.939 --> 01:21:00.232
but, in essence...

625
01:21:00.774 --> 01:21:02.150
Ah...

626
01:21:02.234 --> 01:21:03.777
Hello, Professor,
thanks for seeing me.

627
01:21:03.860 --> 01:21:05.740
My pleasure. You've come at
a good time, Bernie.

628
01:21:05.946 --> 01:21:07.030
This is Phil Hirschkop.

629
01:21:07.113 --> 01:21:08.949
He's a brilliant civil
rights lawyer.

630
01:21:10.784 --> 01:21:11.868
Nice to meet you.

631
01:21:11.952 --> 01:21:13.036
So...

632
01:21:13.620 --> 01:21:15.038
What's the problem?

633
01:21:15.664 --> 01:21:16.831
Well, I'm a bit stumped.

634
01:21:17.791 --> 01:21:19.543
The ACLU referred
me to this case

635
01:21:19.626 --> 01:21:21.002
concerning an
interracial couple

636
01:21:21.086 --> 01:21:22.796
that was married in D.C.

637
01:21:23.296 --> 01:21:25.840
They were arrested for
living together in Virginia,

638
01:21:25.924 --> 01:21:27.551
and the judge suspended
their sentence

639
01:21:27.634 --> 01:21:30.262
under order that they
leave the state for 25 years.

640
01:21:31.179 --> 01:21:34.140
I filed a motion to vacate the
judgment with Judge Bazile,

641
01:21:34.224 --> 01:21:37.060
the original trial judge
in Caroline County,

642
01:21:37.143 --> 01:21:38.311
but he's stonewalling me.

643
01:21:39.312 --> 01:21:43.567
Of course, the ACLU sees this, and
I agree, as a potential contender

644
01:21:43.650 --> 01:21:46.444
to repeal the anti-miscegenation
laws nationwide.

645
01:21:47.988 --> 01:21:50.574
I just need to get the
ball rolling, as it were.

646
01:21:55.245 --> 01:21:57.747
It's a very delicate
situation because by appealing,

647
01:21:57.831 --> 01:22:00.500
you open up the possibility of
sending them both to prison.

648
01:22:01.585 --> 01:22:03.837
I think regardless,
file the 1983 motion

649
01:22:03.920 --> 01:22:05.088
explaining your complaint.

650
01:22:05.171 --> 01:22:06.172
It'll force Bazile's hand

651
01:22:06.256 --> 01:22:08.592
and get you in front of
a federal three-judge panel.

652
01:22:08.675 --> 01:22:09.759
All right.

653
01:22:09.843 --> 01:22:11.362
Look, I got to catch a plane
to New York tonight,

654
01:22:11.386 --> 01:22:13.466
but I'll work up a draft
and I'll find you on Monday?

655
01:22:13.888 --> 01:22:16.600
Great. That's just great.
Thank you.

656
01:22:16.683 --> 01:22:19.769
Yeah. And, Bernie,
if you don't mind me asking,

657
01:22:19.853 --> 01:22:21.104
how much experience
do you have

658
01:22:21.187 --> 01:22:22.397
with constitutional law?

659
01:22:22.814 --> 01:22:24.024
Some.

660
01:22:28.028 --> 01:22:29.487
Very little.

661
01:22:30.864 --> 01:22:32.341
You realize
this case could alter

662
01:22:32.365 --> 01:22:34.159
the constitution of
the United States?

663
01:22:35.869 --> 01:22:36.870
I do.

664
01:22:39.873 --> 01:22:41.041
I'll call you on Monday.

665
01:22:43.043 --> 01:22:45.211
One, two, three!

666
01:22:47.297 --> 01:22:48.548
I'm a good dog!

667
01:22:55.347 --> 01:22:56.699
I can never
get mine to rise.

668
01:22:56.723 --> 01:22:59.392
It's not you.
It's the humidity.

669
01:23:00.185 --> 01:23:01.895
Just thick.

670
01:23:02.062 --> 01:23:03.813
Come look, Meme.
Come look.

671
01:23:03.897 --> 01:23:05.940
Peggy.
She's fine.

672
01:23:06.274 --> 01:23:08.109
What you want
from your Meme?

673
01:23:08.401 --> 01:23:10.570
Lilly won't share
her tea.

674
01:23:12.572 --> 01:23:14.074
She must be upset.

675
01:23:15.492 --> 01:23:17.052
Well, she wants to
sit with us out here.

676
01:23:36.346 --> 01:23:38.181
Momma, get Peggy inside!

677
01:23:40.433 --> 01:23:41.601
Bean!

678
01:23:46.439 --> 01:23:47.941
Hey. What is it?

679
01:23:48.900 --> 01:23:50.360
Well, I got a message for you.

680
01:23:51.778 --> 01:23:52.987
What?

681
01:23:53.071 --> 01:23:55.782
Well, that lawyer called.
Said he wanna meet with y'all.

682
01:23:58.660 --> 01:24:00.870
Sidney! Donald!

683
01:24:02.414 --> 01:24:05.750
Raymond, why you
driving so fast like that?

684
01:24:06.793 --> 01:24:08.628
What you mean?
I always drive like that.

685
01:24:14.676 --> 01:24:15.677
- What?
- Richard.

686
01:24:18.346 --> 01:24:20.640
What is it?
It's okay.

687
01:24:23.101 --> 01:24:26.104
<i>"Almighty God created
the races white, black,</i>

688
01:24:26.187 --> 01:24:27.939
"yellow, Malay, and red,

689
01:24:28.022 --> 01:24:30.567
"and he placed them
on separate continents.

690
01:24:30.650 --> 01:24:32.902
"And but for the interference
with his arrangement

691
01:24:32.986 --> 01:24:35.113
"there would be no cause
for such marriages.

692
01:24:36.322 --> 01:24:37.866
"The fact that he
separated the races

693
01:24:37.949 --> 01:24:40.410
"shows that he did not intend
for the races to mix."

694
01:24:42.662 --> 01:24:44.414
I know it sounds strange,

695
01:24:45.081 --> 01:24:47.000
but this is really wonderful.

696
01:24:47.709 --> 01:24:48.752
By issuing this ruling,

697
01:24:48.835 --> 01:24:50.920
Judge Bazile has really
given us a road map

698
01:24:51.004 --> 01:24:52.672
right to the Supreme Court.

699
01:24:54.841 --> 01:24:56.551
I'm sorry, I'm confused.

700
01:24:57.594 --> 01:24:59.596
He ruled against us again.

701
01:25:00.430 --> 01:25:02.182
That's right, but now
we're allowed to

702
01:25:02.265 --> 01:25:03.725
appeal that ruling
to the state.

703
01:25:03.808 --> 01:25:06.186
From there, if the state
rules against you,

704
01:25:06.478 --> 01:25:08.078
we'll have a chance
at the Supreme Court.

705
01:25:11.316 --> 01:25:12.901
That sounds wonderful.

706
01:25:13.526 --> 01:25:16.279
I have one little piece
of housekeeping.

707
01:25:16.362 --> 01:25:17.947
<i>LIFE</i> magazine contacted us

708
01:25:18.031 --> 01:25:19.949
about sending a photographer
out to you all.

709
01:25:20.033 --> 01:25:23.870
Keeping the possibility of
the Supreme Court in mind,

710
01:25:23.953 --> 01:25:25.747
I think it's a fair idea

711
01:25:25.830 --> 01:25:28.374
that we raise the
profile of your case,

712
01:25:28.458 --> 01:25:31.085
but I, of course,
want to make sure

713
01:25:31.169 --> 01:25:32.837
that you are all
comfortable with that.

714
01:25:39.427 --> 01:25:40.720
It'll be fine.

715
01:25:58.029 --> 01:25:59.280
Hello!

716
01:26:07.747 --> 01:26:09.582
Grey Villet, <i>LIFE</i> magazine.
Pleasure.

717
01:26:11.543 --> 01:26:12.919
What you got there,
a small block?

718
01:26:13.962 --> 01:26:15.004
Yeah. Yeah.

719
01:26:15.088 --> 01:26:16.256
What's the trouble?

720
01:26:17.090 --> 01:26:18.424
Carburetors.

721
01:26:18.508 --> 01:26:19.509
Oh.

722
01:26:20.927 --> 01:26:23.054
Then you're a better
mechanic than me.

723
01:26:24.097 --> 01:26:26.432
If you rejet them,
it goes faster, though, right?

724
01:26:27.725 --> 01:26:29.561
I'm sure you
already know that.

725
01:26:29.686 --> 01:26:31.855
Is your wife inside?

726
01:26:32.272 --> 01:26:33.273
Uh-huh.

727
01:26:40.613 --> 01:26:42.323
Oh. Hello.

728
01:26:43.575 --> 01:26:46.077
Grey Villet.
<i>LIFE</i> magazine.

729
01:26:46.911 --> 01:26:47.912
May I?

730
01:26:47.996 --> 01:26:49.539
Of course. Come in.

731
01:26:51.624 --> 01:26:53.418
Oh. Something smells
good in there.

732
01:26:54.669 --> 01:26:57.755
So, I can't go back without
a photo. No photo, no job.

733
01:26:57.839 --> 01:27:00.717
And this is <i>LIFE</i> magazine and
the pigeon guy isn't around.

734
01:27:00.800 --> 01:27:02.552
- Pigeon guy?
- Pigeon guy?

735
01:27:02.635 --> 01:27:03.761
That's right.

736
01:27:03.845 --> 01:27:06.389
Looking up at this office
building and it hits me.

737
01:27:07.473 --> 01:27:10.602
Right. I go 55 stories up

738
01:27:11.060 --> 01:27:12.395
and I talk some office girls

739
01:27:12.478 --> 01:27:13.980
into letting me look
out the window.

740
01:27:14.355 --> 01:27:16.608
Before they could do anything,
I throw open the window,

741
01:27:16.691 --> 01:27:18.401
sit on the ledge and
dangle my feet out.

742
01:27:19.611 --> 01:27:22.447
They start screaming,
but I got this great shot

743
01:27:22.530 --> 01:27:25.533
of my feet flying over
42nd and 5th Avenue.

744
01:27:26.451 --> 01:27:27.785
Yeah. So what happened?

745
01:27:28.661 --> 01:27:30.914
Security threw me out head first.

746
01:27:31.456 --> 01:27:33.875
But, <i>LIFE</i> magazine
hired me the next day.

747
01:27:35.585 --> 01:27:37.629
That's a story, all right.

748
01:27:37.754 --> 01:27:40.798
Yeah,
that's a story, all right.

749
01:27:45.345 --> 01:27:47.472
You go to the Virginia
State Court next, right?

750
01:27:47.555 --> 01:27:48.765
Yes.

751
01:27:50.850 --> 01:27:52.060
You nervous?

752
01:27:53.019 --> 01:27:54.062
I suppose.

753
01:27:54.145 --> 01:27:55.355
Hmm.

754
01:27:55.438 --> 01:27:57.482
The lawyers told us
not to expect much.

755
01:27:58.691 --> 01:28:00.193
You think you'll lose?

756
01:28:01.235 --> 01:28:02.612
Well, yes.

757
01:28:04.405 --> 01:28:05.949
But I think it's all right.

758
01:28:08.159 --> 01:28:10.870
We may lose the small battles,
but win the big war.

759
01:28:26.219 --> 01:28:27.821
<i>- Coleslaw.
- Yeah.</i>

760
01:28:27.845 --> 01:28:29.847
<i>And here's the surprise.</i>

761
01:28:29.973 --> 01:28:32.016
<i>Some of my new
homemade pickles.</i>

762
01:28:34.811 --> 01:28:37.271
<i>That certainly is
a wonderful surprise.</i>

763
01:28:37.355 --> 01:28:41.067
<i>Look at that, Barney, Aunt Bee's brought
us some of her homemade pickles.</i>

764
01:28:41.150 --> 01:28:43.236
<i>I see.
Sure is wonderful.</i>

765
01:28:43.611 --> 01:28:45.238
<i>You really shouldn't
have, Aunt Bee.</i>

766
01:28:45.321 --> 01:28:46.990
<i>That's right, Aunt Bee.</i>

767
01:28:47.073 --> 01:28:50.576
<i>You go to way yonder too
much trouble to please us.</i>

768
01:28:50.660 --> 01:28:52.787
<i>It's no trouble at all.</i>

769
01:28:52.870 --> 01:28:55.081
<i>There's plenty.
I made eight quarts.</i>

770
01:28:55.248 --> 01:28:56.833
<i>Eight quarts?</i>

771
01:28:56.916 --> 01:29:00.169
<i>Aunt Bee made eight quarts.
Eight quarts.</i>

772
01:29:00.336 --> 01:29:02.422
<i>You can have some every day.</i>

773
01:29:04.215 --> 01:29:06.384
<i>Well, I had an
awful big breakfast.</i>

774
01:29:06.467 --> 01:29:09.012
<i>I just stuffed myself
something fierce.</i>

775
01:29:09.095 --> 01:29:10.763
<i>Have some pickles.</i>

776
01:29:10.847 --> 01:29:11.973
<i>Here you are.</i>

777
01:29:14.058 --> 01:29:16.060
<i>And here you are.</i>

778
01:29:25.111 --> 01:29:26.696
Mr. Loving. Mr. Loving.

779
01:29:26.779 --> 01:29:28.573
They just wanna ask
you a few questions.

780
01:29:31.492 --> 01:29:33.286
Uh... All right.

781
01:29:37.874 --> 01:29:39.876
Mrs. Loving, you rolling?

782
01:29:40.376 --> 01:29:42.128
Mrs. Loving, the
Virginia Supreme Court

783
01:29:42.211 --> 01:29:43.671
just ruled against you.

784
01:29:43.755 --> 01:29:46.007
How do you feel about
what happened here today?

785
01:29:46.924 --> 01:29:48.384
Well, I feel hopeful.

786
01:29:48.968 --> 01:29:50.219
I'm hopeful.

787
01:29:51.054 --> 01:29:52.555
And where will you go now?

788
01:29:54.640 --> 01:29:56.601
Well, I guess we'll go
back to Washington.

789
01:29:56.768 --> 01:29:58.811
You'll go back
to Washington?

790
01:29:58.895 --> 01:30:00.688
Mr. Loving, do you
have anything to say

791
01:30:00.772 --> 01:30:02.648
about what went on
in the court today?

792
01:30:03.066 --> 01:30:04.817
No. I don't have
anything to say.

793
01:30:05.151 --> 01:30:07.111
Okay. Thank you, folks,
very much.

794
01:30:07.403 --> 01:30:08.654
Did you get that?

795
01:30:08.738 --> 01:30:10.990
- I think so.
- Okay, cut, Tommy.

796
01:30:13.659 --> 01:30:14.827
Mr. and Mrs. Loving?

797
01:30:18.498 --> 01:30:19.582
We wanted you to know that,

798
01:30:19.665 --> 01:30:21.876
with all this travel
back and forth from Virginia,

799
01:30:21.959 --> 01:30:24.087
you have my number
and if anybody arrests you,

800
01:30:24.170 --> 01:30:26.130
you have them get
in touch with us.

801
01:30:26.839 --> 01:30:29.258
We're not gonna let you spend
one minute longer in jail

802
01:30:29.342 --> 01:30:32.178
than it takes us to get down
there to get you out, okay?

803
01:30:32.470 --> 01:30:33.930
Okay.

804
01:30:34.013 --> 01:30:35.681
Good luck to you.

805
01:30:35.765 --> 01:30:36.933
You did a good job today.

806
01:30:37.975 --> 01:30:39.894
Well, I sure appreciate
what y'all are doing.

807
01:30:39.977 --> 01:30:41.104
Okay.

808
01:30:41.187 --> 01:30:42.230
Well, we'll see you soon.

809
01:30:42.313 --> 01:30:43.314
Bye.

810
01:30:46.692 --> 01:30:48.236
Thank you, gentlemen.

811
01:30:49.695 --> 01:30:52.281
You know they aren't
going back to Washington.

812
01:30:52.365 --> 01:30:53.550
And there's no
guarantee we can

813
01:30:53.574 --> 01:30:55.493
get them out if they
get arrested again.

814
01:30:56.828 --> 01:30:57.995
Mmm-hmm.

815
01:33:29.855 --> 01:33:30.856
Sidney!

816
01:33:32.984 --> 01:33:34.026
Sidney!

817
01:33:36.696 --> 01:33:38.406
I want you to go next
door to the neighbor.

818
01:33:38.990 --> 01:33:40.467
You gonna ask him
to use the telephone

819
01:33:40.491 --> 01:33:43.369
and you gonna call Raymond and
ask him to bring his gun, okay?

820
01:33:43.452 --> 01:33:45.663
Go. Go on now.
Run through the woods. Go on.

821
01:33:51.502 --> 01:33:52.753
Everything okay?

822
01:33:54.213 --> 01:33:55.339
It's fine.

823
01:33:56.882 --> 01:33:58.009
Richard?

824
01:33:58.092 --> 01:33:59.302
Go on inside.

825
01:34:36.422 --> 01:34:38.758
That truck may have
just been going fishing.

826
01:34:43.387 --> 01:34:44.972
Could be.

827
01:34:46.724 --> 01:34:49.268
You ever hear from anyone
at your work about it?

828
01:34:52.980 --> 01:34:54.607
Not to my face.

829
01:35:02.740 --> 01:35:04.200
Well, I'll tell you this,
Rich,

830
01:35:05.951 --> 01:35:07.953
nobody gonna tell you
what you can't do.

831
01:35:21.384 --> 01:35:22.802
You're all set.

832
01:35:23.969 --> 01:35:24.970
Thank you.

833
01:35:26.138 --> 01:35:27.807
Who we gonna call, Momma?

834
01:35:27.973 --> 01:35:29.850
I don't want you
calling anybody.

835
01:35:31.394 --> 01:35:32.395
How did that go?

836
01:35:32.561 --> 01:35:34.146
Doctor said she'll be fine.

837
01:35:34.313 --> 01:35:35.523
Just put her on aspirin.

838
01:35:36.774 --> 01:35:37.775
Who was that?

839
01:35:38.359 --> 01:35:39.735
Telephone man.

840
01:35:40.486 --> 01:35:42.071
Richard had him
install a phone.

841
01:35:43.322 --> 01:35:44.532
Momma, you feel okay?

842
01:35:44.657 --> 01:35:45.658
Yes.

843
01:35:45.741 --> 01:35:47.785
You got some tea I can drink?
Mmm-hmm.

844
01:35:47.868 --> 01:35:48.869
All right.

845
01:36:11.517 --> 01:36:14.854
Testing, testing. Testing.

846
01:36:17.731 --> 01:36:20.025
What do you think
you would do if you...

847
01:36:20.109 --> 01:36:21.360
If you lose the case?

848
01:36:23.779 --> 01:36:25.030
Well...

849
01:36:26.323 --> 01:36:27.324
If we lose,

850
01:36:28.200 --> 01:36:30.536
then we would have to
go back to Washington.

851
01:36:31.579 --> 01:36:32.788
And how does
that make you feel

852
01:36:32.872 --> 01:36:34.331
having to go back
to Washington?

853
01:36:34.415 --> 01:36:36.000
Mildred?

854
01:36:40.504 --> 01:36:41.505
Come here.

855
01:36:47.428 --> 01:36:48.554
Excuse me.
Yeah.

856
01:37:02.318 --> 01:37:03.777
I don't want those
people here.

857
01:37:04.612 --> 01:37:06.071
I'm done with
all these cameras!

858
01:37:07.114 --> 01:37:08.532
Well, I think it's important.

859
01:37:11.076 --> 01:37:13.078
These people want
to help us, Richard.

860
01:37:38.729 --> 01:37:39.730
Well, actually,

861
01:37:39.813 --> 01:37:42.233
although I'm sure the
publicity isn't very pleasant,

862
01:37:43.025 --> 01:37:44.235
if it works out for you,

863
01:37:44.610 --> 01:37:46.529
it will work out for
a lot of other people, too.

864
01:37:47.112 --> 01:37:48.113
Yes.

865
01:37:49.323 --> 01:37:50.324
I hope so.

866
01:37:51.909 --> 01:37:53.494
It's the principle.

867
01:37:53.577 --> 01:37:55.538
It's the law.
I don't think it's right.

868
01:37:56.580 --> 01:37:59.416
And if... If we do win,

869
01:37:59.792 --> 01:38:01.502
we will be helping
a lot of people.

870
01:38:02.503 --> 01:38:03.754
Mmm-hmm.

871
01:38:05.089 --> 01:38:08.008
And I knew...
I know we have some enemies,

872
01:38:08.217 --> 01:38:09.802
but we have some friends,
too.

873
01:38:11.804 --> 01:38:13.430
So it really don't
make a difference

874
01:38:14.265 --> 01:38:15.349
about my enemies.

875
01:38:34.493 --> 01:38:35.995
Push in hard on that one.

876
01:38:36.078 --> 01:38:37.438
You go straight
down the way, okay?

877
01:38:37.496 --> 01:38:39.096
I got it. I got it.
Don't worry about it.

878
01:38:39.123 --> 01:38:40.249
Hey. Good ride.
All right.

879
01:38:40.332 --> 01:38:42.060
Make sure you get it into
second as quick as you can.

880
01:38:42.084 --> 01:38:43.524
- You got it.
- All right.

881
01:38:57.850 --> 01:38:59.310
Car looks good.

882
01:38:59.393 --> 01:39:00.769
Yeah, it's running all right.

883
01:39:04.189 --> 01:39:06.317
You see him
driving today.

884
01:39:06.400 --> 01:39:08.861
It was like he was sitting
in the back seat.

885
01:39:16.952 --> 01:39:20.122
Oh, man. I miss you, Rich.

886
01:39:20.205 --> 01:39:21.915
Hell, I can say it.

887
01:39:21.999 --> 01:39:23.292
Hey, Percy,
don't you miss Rich?

888
01:39:23.626 --> 01:39:24.710
Yeah.

889
01:39:26.170 --> 01:39:27.796
I miss you too, Virgil.

890
01:39:30.424 --> 01:39:33.135
Man. So, what's all this
you got going?

891
01:39:34.136 --> 01:39:35.846
All what?
What you got.

892
01:39:36.263 --> 01:39:38.349
You just went
made it hard now.

893
01:39:38.891 --> 01:39:40.768
No, no. You think I'm crazy,

894
01:39:40.851 --> 01:39:42.561
but you know what
hard is now, don't you?

895
01:39:43.687 --> 01:39:44.688
Yeah.

896
01:39:45.648 --> 01:39:47.066
Richard, you are white.

897
01:39:49.401 --> 01:39:51.862
Now, you may think you're like
a black man, but you're white.

898
01:39:52.571 --> 01:39:54.049
You hang around
all these black folks,

899
01:39:54.073 --> 01:39:56.075
but when you go to work,
you're still white.

900
01:39:57.242 --> 01:39:58.410
But not now.

901
01:39:59.286 --> 01:40:01.413
Now you know what it feels
like now, don't you?

902
01:40:03.499 --> 01:40:05.417
You're black now, ain't you?

903
01:40:06.085 --> 01:40:08.253
You're a damn fool.
All right, come on now.

904
01:40:08.921 --> 01:40:10.464
No, he needs to hear it.

905
01:40:11.465 --> 01:40:13.884
Look, every nigga in here
wish they were you, Rich,

906
01:40:14.301 --> 01:40:16.011
and you ain't got
sense enough for it.

907
01:40:16.428 --> 01:40:18.847
You got a fix.
I ain't got no fix.

908
01:40:19.765 --> 01:40:21.475
So yours is easy.

909
01:40:21.558 --> 01:40:23.018
All you gotta do
is divorce her.

910
01:40:24.228 --> 01:40:25.521
Divorce her?

911
01:40:25.604 --> 01:40:27.356
All you gotta do.

912
01:40:30.943 --> 01:40:32.486
Yeah.
Yeah. Really.

913
01:40:34.405 --> 01:40:35.989
- I'm gonna divorce her.
- That it.

914
01:40:37.783 --> 01:40:39.535
That's all
you gotta do, right?

915
01:40:39.618 --> 01:40:41.203
That's all you gotta do.

916
01:40:47.459 --> 01:40:48.877
Apologize now, Virgil.

917
01:41:47.478 --> 01:41:48.687
Come to bed, Richard.

918
01:41:51.815 --> 01:41:53.275
We've been

919
01:41:54.735 --> 01:41:56.945
talking to lawyers for

920
01:41:59.364 --> 01:42:01.033
near 10 years now.

921
01:42:11.376 --> 01:42:12.419
Let's go to bed.

922
01:42:17.758 --> 01:42:19.343
I can take care of you.

923
01:42:23.347 --> 01:42:24.389
I know that.

924
01:42:34.733 --> 01:42:36.318
I can take care of you.

925
01:42:44.952 --> 01:42:45.994
I know.

926
01:42:49.915 --> 01:42:52.835
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

927
01:42:53.627 --> 01:42:54.628
It's okay.

928
01:43:54.605 --> 01:43:55.981
It's very good.

929
01:43:58.942 --> 01:44:00.903
Well, I have some
really terrific news.

930
01:44:01.695 --> 01:44:03.780
The Supreme Court has agreed
to hear our case.

931
01:44:05.073 --> 01:44:08.201
Now, of course, the state of
Virginia will mount their defense,

932
01:44:08.702 --> 01:44:10.913
but we are feeling very good
about our chances here.

933
01:44:10.996 --> 01:44:13.624
You've got the full weight
of the ACLU behind this.

934
01:44:15.959 --> 01:44:17.502
It's a miracle.
Hmm.

935
01:44:20.005 --> 01:44:21.340
What's their defense?

936
01:44:22.799 --> 01:44:23.842
I'm sorry?

937
01:44:24.009 --> 01:44:25.344
Virginia.

938
01:44:27.012 --> 01:44:29.681
How are they gonna defend
what they done to us?

939
01:44:31.266 --> 01:44:33.143
I guess we won't know
until the hearing,

940
01:44:33.226 --> 01:44:35.562
but it's likely
that they'll use

941
01:44:35.646 --> 01:44:38.190
a defense similar to something
they've used before.

942
01:44:39.816 --> 01:44:41.109
What's that?

943
01:44:48.158 --> 01:44:49.201
It's your kids.

944
01:44:53.538 --> 01:44:54.581
Our kids?

945
01:44:59.294 --> 01:45:02.297
The state of Virginia
will argue that it is unfair

946
01:45:02.381 --> 01:45:04.967
to bring children
of mixed race into the world.

947
01:45:09.388 --> 01:45:11.556
They believe
the children are bastards.

948
01:45:23.610 --> 01:45:25.654
Now, as the defendants
in this trial,

949
01:45:25.737 --> 01:45:28.323
you are allowed to come
and hear the arguments.

950
01:45:32.411 --> 01:45:34.997
No. We don't need to do that.

951
01:45:37.040 --> 01:45:40.836
It's a tremendous honor to sit with
the Supreme Court. Very few people...

952
01:45:40.919 --> 01:45:42.087
No.

953
01:45:45.507 --> 01:45:46.591
That's fine.

954
01:45:48.844 --> 01:45:49.886
Excuse me.

955
01:46:03.275 --> 01:46:04.317
Mildred?

956
01:46:09.614 --> 01:46:11.533
I wouldn't go without him.

957
01:46:36.975 --> 01:46:40.353
You know, Richard, it's, of course,
up to you not to attend but,

958
01:46:41.980 --> 01:46:46.693
you should know, the Supreme Court
only hears one out of every 400 cases.

959
01:46:47.486 --> 01:46:48.528
It's historic.

960
01:46:55.827 --> 01:46:56.995
Thank you, Mr. Cohen.

961
01:46:58.997 --> 01:47:01.708
Well. Is there anything
you'd like me to say to them?

962
01:47:03.835 --> 01:47:07.464
And by "them" I mean the Supreme
Court justices of the United States?

963
01:47:16.014 --> 01:47:17.057
Yeah.

964
01:47:22.437 --> 01:47:23.480
You can tell the judge...

965
01:47:27.275 --> 01:47:29.194
Tell the judge
I love my wife.

966
01:48:10.402 --> 01:48:12.904
You okay to park?
Thanks, Martha.

967
01:48:20.579 --> 01:48:22.330
<i>Number 395.</i>

968
01:48:24.082 --> 01:48:28.336
Richard Perry Loving
et al, Appellants,

969
01:48:29.671 --> 01:48:31.298
v. Virginia.

970
01:48:38.638 --> 01:48:40.056
<i>Mr. Hirschkop.</i>

971
01:48:50.984 --> 01:48:53.904
Mr. Chief Justice, Associate Justices,
may it please the court?

972
01:48:57.782 --> 01:48:59.701
<i>You have before you today</i>

973
01:49:00.619 --> 01:49:03.246
<i>what we consider
the most odious</i>

974
01:49:03.330 --> 01:49:05.916
<i>of the segregation laws
and the slavery laws,</i>

975
01:49:05.999 --> 01:49:09.127
<i>and our view of this law,
and we hope to clearly show,</i>

976
01:49:10.962 --> 01:49:12.714
<i>is that this is a slavery law.</i>

977
01:49:15.884 --> 01:49:19.512
<i>We ask that the Court consider
the full spectrum of these laws</i>

978
01:49:19.596 --> 01:49:20.889
<i>and not just the criminality,</i>

979
01:49:20.972 --> 01:49:25.060
<i>because it's more than criminality
that's at point here.</i>

980
01:49:26.478 --> 01:49:28.021
<i>It's the right
to inherit land,</i>

981
01:49:29.689 --> 01:49:31.441
<i>the legitimacy of children,</i>

982
01:49:32.484 --> 01:49:33.985
<i>and many, many rights.</i>

983
01:49:36.821 --> 01:49:37.906
<i>Mr. Cohen.</i>

984
01:49:46.539 --> 01:49:48.375
Mr. Chief Justice,
may it please the court?

985
01:49:50.794 --> 01:49:53.380
What is the danger
to the state of Virginia

986
01:49:53.505 --> 01:49:55.090
<i>of interracial marriage?</i>

987
01:50:01.179 --> 01:50:04.349
<i>What is the state of
danger to the people</i>

988
01:50:04.432 --> 01:50:06.226
<i>of interracial marriage?</i>

989
01:50:09.813 --> 01:50:11.189
<i>Marriage</i>

990
01:50:12.524 --> 01:50:14.192
<i>is a fundamental right.</i>

991
01:51:29.851 --> 01:51:30.852
Hello?

992
01:51:32.437 --> 01:51:33.938
<i>Mrs. Loving?</i>
Yes.

993
01:51:34.314 --> 01:51:35.607
<i>It's Bernard Cohen.</i>

994
01:51:36.441 --> 01:51:37.942
Oh, hello, Mr. Cohen.

995
01:51:38.860 --> 01:51:41.196
<i>I'm calling with great news.</i>

996
01:51:41.279 --> 01:51:43.615
<i>Just wanted to let you know.</i>
What's that?

997
01:51:53.249 --> 01:51:54.292
Yes, I'm here.

998
01:51:57.253 --> 01:51:58.630
That's wonderful news.

999
01:52:02.258 --> 01:52:03.760
Yes, I understand.

1000
01:52:09.599 --> 01:52:10.642
Okay.

1001
01:52:12.936 --> 01:52:14.437
Thank you, Mr. Cohen.

1002
01:53:06.614 --> 01:53:08.241
Mr. Loving? Mr. Loving?

1003
01:53:08.658 --> 01:53:10.898
Mr. Loving, how does it feel
to have the Supreme Court...

1004
01:53:11.369 --> 01:53:13.222
Have you heard
from the Attorney General?

1005
01:53:13.246 --> 01:53:15.331
Mrs. Loving, what does
this mean to your family?

1006
01:53:15.415 --> 01:53:17.125
Do you plan
to return to Virginia?

1007
01:53:18.168 --> 01:53:19.752
Have you talked to
the Attorney General?

1008
01:53:20.712 --> 01:53:23.923
Several Southern states
have already announced this ruling...

1009
01:53:39.355 --> 01:53:40.899
Take that to your daddy.

1010
01:53:51.659 --> 01:53:52.660
Oh.

1011
01:53:54.412 --> 01:53:55.747
Wanna help me?
Mmm-hmm.

1012
01:53:57.499 --> 01:53:58.958
You wanna brush the wall?
